The world wide leader in professional wrestling, the WWF became the top promotion in the world after the 1980s boom period that was led by Hulk Hogan and Wrestlemania. Owned by Vince McMahon, the WWF crippled the territory system of the 80s and ran nearly all of its competition out of business. Now standing at the top of the industry, opposed by only WCW, Vince McMahon's WWF seems to be an unstoppable titan.
